      "statusChangeID": null,
      "value": "@{6330c3498a42be44a9d028c6|full_name}: It's likely that your login session has been caught in a bad state, please see the instructions below. If you continue experiencing issues after following these steps contact the support team at: https://vrch.at/support\nIf you cannot successfully launch into ANY VRChat world:\nVRChat on Meta Quest\nUninstall VRChat from your headset completely, and re-install it. This will clear all of your settings.\nVRChat on PC\nGo to this Help article and follow the steps under Automatic Mode: https://help.vrchat.com/hc/en-us/articles/1500002247921-VRChat-keeps-crashing-or-has-issues-launching-properly\nIf you have configured an alternate cache location in your config.json you must go clear your cache manually.\n---\nIf you can successfully get into VRChat:\n1. Press B to open your Quick Menu\n2. Click the \"expand\" icon in the top right of the Quick Menu to open the Main Menu\n3. Go to \"Settings\"\n4. Go to \"Advanced Settings\" in the top right\n5. Click all three buttons. Click \"Clear Profile Data\" last.\n6. You will be logged out. Exit out of VRChat and relaunch.\nLive Beta Users:\n1. Press B to open your Quick Menu\n2. Click the \"expand\" icon in the top right of the Quick Menu to open the Main Menu\n3. Click the \"Gear\" tab on the bottom of the Main Menu\n4. Click \"Performance\" on the left side\n5. Scroll down to \"Manage Cached Data\" and click \"Clear Content Cache\"\n6. Click \"Debug\" on the left side\n7. Click \"Clear Local Profile Data\"\n8. You will be logged out. Exit out of VRChat and relaunch.",
      "viewerReactions": null,
      "voteID": null
    },
